Hypothesis: Info 17011 "WYSIWYG SPI primitive miso_in converted to
equivalent logic" caused by Quartus optimizing away the asmiblock's
data0out path due to single-fanout pattern.  Tested by adding
(* keep = 1, noprune *) attribute on miso_in wire AND
(* preserve, noprune *) on u_asmi instance.

Result: REFUTED.  Info 17011 still fires; message now identifies
"u_asmi" instead of "miso_in" (the attribute moved the report
target to the instance itself, confirming the conversion is at
INSTANCE level, not net level).  HW capture md5
50f8a01703e391aaa83054909e9b6eec — byte-IDENTICAL to v1+v2 across all
3 builds.  Phase E addrs 0..3 still all return 0xff.

**Final verdict on Plan B**: hand-rolled SPI master against
cycloneive_asmiblock primitive is architecturally INFEASIBLE in
Quartus 21.1 Lite + Cyclone IV E + INTERNAL_FLASH_UPDATE_MODE=REMOTE.
The toolchain reduces hand-instantiated asmiblock cells to equivalent
combinational logic that does NOT route to the silicon AS pins,
regardless of attribute hints (keep, noprune, preserve).  The only
known path to AS-pin access in this toolchain is via the
altasmi_parallel megafunction (epcs_ctrl.v), which itself has
internal pipeline timing races that NH15+NH16-fw+NH17 wrapper-layer
patches could not eliminate.

Both wrapper paths exhausted; Phase 3 content-read closure requires
either: (a) toolchain change (Quartus Pro / different version), (b)
firmware-side approach using altasmi but with different pacing
strategy (e.g., wrapping altasmi with a FIFO + length counter to
break the megafunction's internal stream-overflow), or (c) deferring
Phase 3 to focus on Phase 6/9 progress while content-read remains
PARTIAL (blank-flash detect already silicon-closed via NH10).
---
 rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v b/rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v
index 4eecb1d..c43c2d4 100644
--- a/rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v
+++ b/rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v
@@ -181,7 +181,14 @@ module wb_altasmi_parallel (
     // Outputs to the asmiblock primitive.
     reg cs_n_q;
     reg mosi_q;
-    wire miso_in;
+    // Plan B v3 (2026-05-18): explicit (* keep *) on miso_in to test
+    // whether Info 17011 "WYSIWYG SPI primitive miso_in converted to
+    // equivalent logic" in Plan B v1+v2 was caused by Quartus optimizing
+    // away the asmiblock primitive's data0out path.  altasmi-based
+    // builds don't trigger 17011; hand-rolled v1+v2 do and produce
+    // all-0xff reads.  This attribute forces Quartus to preserve the
+    // wire as a real net rather than fold it into combinational logic.
+    (* keep = 1, noprune *) wire miso_in;
 
     // oe MUST be tied to a constant 1'b0 for the asmiblock primitive to
     // be preserved by Quartus 21.1 Lite as a hardware cell rather than
@@ -428,7 +435,7 @@ module wb_altasmi_parallel (
     // 5-port single-bit SPI to dedicated AS pins
     // (cycloneive_atoms.v line 7017).  oe=0 → user logic drives DCLK
     // / nCSO / ASDO; data0out reads DATA0 (MISO).
-    cycloneive_asmiblock u_asmi (
+    (* preserve, noprune *) cycloneive_asmiblock u_asmi (
         .dclkin   (sck_q),
         .scein    (cs_n_q),
         .oe       (oe_const),
